Ferris spoke into the limitless emptiness, and it was the truest thing he
said. Maybe he would have torn it up. Maybe he never would have accepted
it. But just maybe, he wouldn’t have done either. Just maybe, they would have

had a chance to talk to each other.
With a gentle sigh, Ferris looked at Hannah. She looked back at him, still
holding the limp form of the husband she had strangled, and smiled again.
Then her smile fell—literally—as she crumbled into a pile of powdery
